-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC #### C3.2 Table Migration
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC During installation, you'll be prompted with regards to how to handle tables; in particular, how to handle managed tables with external locations. This is a common pattern, and an easy one to optimize during the upgrade. In this section, we demystify the options.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ##### C3.2.1 Convert to external and migrate as external
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Converting a managed HMS table to external is a simple, low-impact operation. HMS will still be able to read/write the data. Meanwhile, we create a similar external table in the UC metastore referencing the same data; UC will also be able to read/write the data. So now we have two instances of the table referring to the same underlying data. The important benefit of this arrangement is that no updates can be lost during the transition period, if legacy workloads continue to operate on the HMS table.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC The main reason for converting the HMS table to external is to unhook *data lifecycle management*. So when we ultimately drop the table or get rid of HMS altogether, the data files will not be touched.
-- MAGIC
