-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ##### C3.2.2 Migrate as external
-- MAGIC This approach is similar to the previously mentioned approach: create an external table in the UC metastore referencing the same data as the HMS table. So now we have two instances of the table referring to the same underlying data, ensuring that no updates can be lost during the transition period, if legacy workloads continue to operate on the HMS table.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC The main difference with this option is that we're skipping the step that converts the source HMS table to external. 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 8px solid #ff9800; background: #fff3e0; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 4px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">⚠️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       This option is more dangerous, because the HMS table still manages the data lifecycle. Dropping the table in HMS would result in destruction of the underlying data, rendering the UC table unusable. So eventually, you should convert the HMS table to external to avoid this.
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>
