-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ##### C3.2.3 Copy as managed
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC This approach simply creates a new managed table in the UC metastore based on the table in the HMS metastore, using CTAS or similarly spirited operation. This results in copying the table data as well.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC There are two downsides to be aware of with this approach:
-- MAGIC - For large tables, this results in a large movement of copy, which could potentially be time-consuming (and expensive if the operation incurs egress charges)
-- MAGIC - Results in two independent copies of the table data. If legacy workloads continue to make changes to the HMS table, those changes would not be reflected in UC (and vice versa) unless you periodically synchronize the two
